    "message": "fix(updates): use CREATE_NO_WINDOW so the Windows update helper actually runs\n\nThe deferred helper was spawned with DETACHED_PROCESS, which denies the child a\nconsole. powershell.exe then exits immediately without running the script, so\nthe staged update silently never installed and no result was ever recorded --\nthe update simply appeared to do nothing.\n\nMeasured across creation-flag variants with everything else held constant:\n\n    DETACHED_PROCESS | CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP   ran=False\n    CREATE_NO_WINDOW | CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP   ran=True\n    CREATE_NO_WINDOW                              ran=True\n    CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP                      ran=True\n    (no flags)                                    ran=True\n\nCREATE_NO_WINDOW keeps a console the child can use while hiding it, and the new\nprocess group still keeps the helper from being signalled with the console the\nserver was started from. Survival across parent exit was confirmed separately:\nthe helper waits for the parent pid to disappear and then completes.\n\nVerified unattended, end to end, in an isolated UV_TOOL_DIR with nothing\nstubbed: the running environment stages the wheel, the process exits, and the\nhelper installs on its own -- ok=true, exit_code=0, environment moved 4.21.4 ->\n4.21.3 with the entry point working afterwards.\n\nThe earlier attempts were tested with the spawn stubbed or the script run by\nhand, which is exactly why two separate defects (the NativeCommandError and\nthis one) both survived review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
